# 22. Responsive Design

The website has dedicated:

* Desktop layouts
* Mobile layouts
* Responsive components
* Mobile-specific content structures
* Responsive navigation/CTA behavior
* Sticky mobile/footer behavior

Examples include separate classes such as:

```text
about-desktop
about-mobile

learn-desktop
learn-mobile

mentor-desktop
mentor-mobile
```

This structure allows the page to provide different layouts and information density depending on screen size.

---

# 23. Visual Design System

The website uses a dark, modern education/career aesthetic.

Important CSS variables referenced throughout the HTML include:

```css
var(--color-primary)
var(--color-text-muted)
```

The primary accent is consistently used for:

* Icons
* Highlights
* Important text
* CTA elements
* Section accents

The page uses **Inter** as its Google Font.

---

# 24. Icons

The website primarily uses inline SVG icons.

Icons are used for:

* Calendar
* Live session/video
* AI/technology
* Career direction
* Documents
* Mentorship
* Business/startups
* Time/countdown
* Testimonials
* Navigation arrows
* Benefits

This keeps the icon system lightweight without requiring a separate icon library.

---

# 25. Calls to Action

The primary conversion action appears throughout the website using variations of:

* Claim Now
* Claim Your Seat
* Join for ₹999/-
* Join the Workshop
* Register Now

The CTA strategy is intentionally repeated across major sections so visitors can register without having to return to the top of the page.

